the core classes, functions, methods that will be necessary, as well as a quick comment on their purpose.\nThen you will call the functions provided to firstly create Python venv, and then install packages. After that, you should implement the codes and call the functions to save them. \nNote: the code should be equipped with doc, such as:\n\n\n"""\nThis is the main module to launch the program\n"""\nfrom server import run\n\nif __name__ == "__main__":\n    run()\n\n\nPlease note that the code should be fully functional. Ensure to implement all functions. No placeholders (such as \'pass\' in Python).\nYou should call the provided functions to save your code.To accomplish the task of constructing and evaluating a TextCNN model using PyTorch for text classification, we can structure the project into several core components. Below is the outline of the necessary classes, functions, and their purposes:\n\n### Core Classes and Functions\n\n1. **DataLoader**:\n   - Purpose: To handle data loading and preprocessing, including tokenization and padding of text input.\n\n2. **TextCNN**:\n   - Purpose: To define the architecture of the TextCNN model including convolutional layers, activation functions, and fully connected layers.\n\n3. **Trainer**:\n   - Purpose: To manage the training process, including forward pass, loss calculation, backpropagation, and model evaluation.\n\n4. **Evaluator**:\n   - Purpose: To evaluate the model\'s performance on a validation/test set and compute accuracy.\n\n5. **main**:\n   - Purpose: The entry point of the program which orchestrates data loading, model training, and evaluation.\n\n### Steps to Implement\n\n1. Create a Python virtual environment.\n2. Install necessary packages such as `torch`, `torchvision`, `numpy`, `pandas`, and `scikit-learn`.\n3. Implement the classes and functions as outlined above.\n4. Save the code files.\n\n### Code Structure\n\nWe will create the following files:\n- `dataloader.py`: Contains the `DataLoader` class.\n- `textcnn.py`: Contains the `TextCNN` class.\n- `trainer.py`: Contains the `Trainer` class.\n- `evaluator.py`: Contains the `Evaluator` class.\n- `main.py`: The main entry point for the program.\n\n### Creating the Virtual Environment and Installing Packages\n\nFirst, let\'s create the Python virtual environment and install the required packages. \n\nI\'ll go ahead and execute this.Tool init_python_env error: uv command not found in PATHTool init_python_env error: uv command not found in PATHTool install_python_packages error: uv command not found in PATHIt seems there is an issue with the virtual environment setup and package installation commands. However, I will proceed to implement the code structure, and we can handle the environment setup afterward.\n\n### Implementation of the Code Files\n\n1. **dataloader.py**\n   ```python\n   """\n   This module handles data loading and preprocessing for the TextCNN model.\n   """\n   import pandas as pd\n   from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n   from sklearn.preprocessing import LabelEncoder\n   from torch.utils.data import Dataset, DataLoader\n   from torchvision import transforms\n   import torch\n\n   class TextDataset(Dataset):\n       def __init__(self, texts, labels):\n           self.texts = texts\n           self.labels = labels\n\n       def __len__(self):\n           return len(self.texts)\n\n       def __getitem__(self, idx):\n           return self.texts[idx], self.labels[idx]\n\n   class DataLoader:\n       def __init__(self, file_path):\n           self.file_path = file_path\n\n       def load_data(self):\n           data = pd.read_csv(self.file_path)\n           label_encoder = LabelEncoder()\n           data[\'label\'] = label_encoder.fit_transform(data[\'label\'])\n           texts = data[\'text\'].tolist()\n           labels = data[\'label\'].tolist()\n           return train_test_split(texts, labels, test_size=0.2, random_state=42)\n   ```\n\n2. **textcnn.py**\n   ```python\n   """\n   This module defines the TextCNN architecture for text classification.\n   """\n   import torch\n   import torch.nn as nn\n\n   class TextCNN(nn.Module):\n       def __init__(self, vocab_size, embedding_dim, num_classes):\n           super(TextCNN, self).__init__()\n           self.embedding = nn.Embedding(vocab_size, embedding_dim)\n           self.conv1 = nn.Conv2d(1, 100, (3, embedding_dim))\n           self.conv2 = nn.Conv2d(1, 100, (4, embedding_dim))\n           self.conv3 = nn.Conv2d(1, 100, (5, embedding_dim))\n           self.fc = nn.Linear(300, num_classes)\n           self.dropout = nn.Dropout(0.5)\n\n       def forward(self, x):\n           x = self.embedding(x).unsqueeze(1)\n           x1 = self.conv1(x).squeeze(3)\n           x2 = self.conv2(x).squeeze(3)\n           x3 = self.conv3(x).squeeze(3)\n           x1 = nn.functional.relu(x1)\n           x2 = nn.functional.relu(x2)\n           x3 = nn.functional.relu(x3)\n           x1 = nn.functional.max_pool1d(x1, x1.size(2)).view(x1.size(0), -1)\n           x2 = nn.functional.max_pool1d(x2, x2.size(2)).view(x2.size(0), -1)\n           x3 = nn.functional.max_pool1d(x3, x3.size(2)).view(x3.size(0), -1)\n           x = torch.cat((x1, x2, x3), 1)\n           x = self.dropout(x)\n           return self.fc(x)\n   ```\n\n3. **trainer.py**\n   ```python\n   """\n   This module manages the training process for the TextCNN model.\n   """\n   import torch\n   import torch.optim as optim\n   import torch.nn.functional as F\n\n   class Trainer:\n       def __init__(self, model, train_loader, val_loader, num_epochs=10):\n           self.model = model\n           self.train_loader = train_loader\n           self.val_loader = val_loader\n           self.num_epochs = num_epochs\n           self.optimizer = optim.Adam(model.parameters())\n\n       def train(self):\n           for epoch in range(self.num_epochs):\n               self.model.train()\n               for texts, labels in self.train_loader:\n                   self.optimizer.zero_grad()\n                   outputs = self.model(texts)\n                   loss = F.cross_entropy(outputs, labels)\n                   loss.backward()\n                   self.optimizer.step()\n\n       def evaluate(self):\n           self.model.eval()\n           correct = 0\n           total = 0\n           with torch.no_grad():\n               for texts, labels in self.val_loader:\n                   outputs = self.model(texts)\n                   _, predicted = torch.max(outputs.data, 1)\n                   total += labels.size(0)\n                   correct += (predicted == labels).sum().item()\n           return correct / total\n   ```\n\n4. **evaluator.py**\n   ```python\n   """\n   This module evaluates the performance of the TextCNN model.\n   """\n   class Evaluator:\n       def __init__(self, model, data_loader):\n           self.model = model\n           self.data_loader = data_loader\n\n       def compute_accuracy(self):\n           correct = 0\n           total = 0\n           with torch.no_grad():\n               for texts, labels in self.data_loader:\n                   outputs = self.model(texts)\n                   _, predicted = torch.max(outputs.data, 1)\n                   total += labels.size(0)\n                   correct += (predicted == labels).sum().item()\n           return correct / total\n   ```\n\n5. **main.py**\n   ```python\n   """\n   This is the main module to launch the program.\n   """\n   from dataloader import DataLoader\n   from textcnn import TextCNN\n   from trainer import Trainer\n\n   if __name__ == "__main__":\n       data_loader = DataLoader("data.csv")\n       train_texts, val_texts, train_labels, val_labels = data_loader.load_data()\n       \n       # Create DataLoader instances\n       train_dataset = TextDataset(train_texts, train_labels)\n       val_dataset = TextDataset(val_texts, val_labels)\n       train_loader = DataLoader(train_dataset, batch_size=32, shuffle=True)\n       val_loader = DataLoader(val_dataset, batch_size=32)\n\n       # Initialize model\n       model = TextCNN(vocab_size=10000, embedding_dim=300, num_classes=10)\n\n       # Train and evaluate\n       trainer = Trainer(model, train_loader, val_loader)\n       trainer.train()\n       accuracy = trainer.evaluate()\n       print(f"Validation Accuracy: {accuracy:.2f}")\n   ```\n\n### Saving the Code Files\n\nNow, I will save the implemented code files in the workspace.{\n  "path": "dataloader.py",\n  "absolute_path": "C:\\\\Users\\\\lucag\\\\SwarmDev_Parallel\\\\ChatDev\\\\WareHouse\\\\TextCNN_20260531150239\\\\code_workspace\\\\dataloader.py",\n  "size": 980\n}{\n  "path": "textcnn.py",\n  "absolute_path": "C:\\\\Users\\\\lucag\\\\SwarmDev_Parallel\\\\ChatDev\\\\WareHouse\\\\TextCNN_20260531150239\\\\code_workspace\\\\textcnn.py",\n  "size": 1180\n}{\n  "path": "trainer.py",\n  "absolute_path": "C:\\\\Users\\\\lucag\\\\SwarmDev_Parallel\\\\ChatDev\\\\WareHouse\\\\TextCNN_20260531150239\\\\code_workspace\\\\trainer.py",\n  "size": 1197\n}{\n  "path": "evaluator.py",\n  "absolute_path": "C:\\\\Users\\\\lucag\\\\SwarmDev_Parallel\\\\ChatDev\\\\WareHouse\\\\TextCNN_20260531150239\\\\code_workspace\\\\evaluator.py",\n  "size": 581\n}{\n  "path": "main.py",\n  "absolute_path": "C:\\\\Users\\\\lucag\\\\SwarmDev_Parallel\\\\ChatDev\\\\WareHouse\\\\TextCNN_20260531150239\\\\code_workspace\\\\main.py",\n  "size": 855\n}', 'output': None, 'input_size': 10871, 'output_size': 0, 'stage': 'before'} 
