 import preprocess_data\n   data = preprocess_data('path/to/your/data')\n   ```\n\n2. **Train the Model**: Set up the model and begin training with your preprocessed data.\n   ```python\n   from model import TextCNN\n   model = TextCNN()\n   model.train(data)\n   ```\n\n3. **Evaluate the Model**: After training, evaluate the model's performance on a test dataset to obtain accuracy.\n   ```python\n   accuracy = model.evaluate('path/to/test/data')\n   print(f'Model Accuracy: {accuracy}')\n   ```\n\n4. **Adjust Hyperparameters**: You may want to adjust hyperparameters such as learning rate, batch size, etc., in the model configuration to improve performance.\n\n## Conclusion\nThis user manual provides an overview of how to set up and use the TextCNN model for text classification. Refer to the code documentation for detailed information on specific functions and their parameters.", 'encoding': 'utf-8', 'mode': 'overwrite'}, 'stage': 'before'} 
